WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:03.853
It was a cloudy day.

2
00:00:03.854 --> 00:00:08.271
The kids looked out the window as they put on their aprons.

3
00:00:08.272 --> 00:00:12.091
"A storm is coming," Jason said.

4
00:00:12.092 --> 00:00:16.556
"Oh no!" Izzie thought.

5
00:00:16.557 --> 00:00:19.876
"Everyone, pay attention," Chef said.

6
00:00:19.877 --> 00:00:23.376
"We're making beef chili today."

7
00:00:23.377 --> 00:00:29.201
Outside, lightning flashed, followed by a rumble of thunder.

8
00:00:29.202 --> 00:00:31.637
Izzie clenched her teeth.

9
00:00:31.638 --> 00:00:36.451
"Yay! It's starting to rain!" Nina said.

10
00:00:36.452 --> 00:00:40.364
"The garden is getting watered!"

11
00:00:40.365 --> 00:00:45.022
Chef nodded. "Jason, please chop the onion.

12
00:00:45.023 --> 00:00:47.958
Izzie, you can chop the bell pepper.

13
00:00:47.959 --> 00:00:53.254
Bobby and Nina, you can chop the garlic."

14
00:00:53.255 --> 00:00:57.586
Izzie tried not to look out the window as she worked.

15
00:00:57.587 --> 00:01:02.095
When she was finished, she checked the recipe again.

16
00:01:02.096 --> 00:01:06.645
"Next we cook the pepper and onion."

17
00:01:06.646 --> 00:01:11.948
Nina poured oil into a pot and added the pepper and onion.

18
00:01:11.949 --> 00:01:14.437
Bobby added the garlic.

19
00:01:14.438 --> 00:01:16.687
Lightning flashed again.

20
00:01:16.688 --> 00:01:21.489
Boom! This time the thunder was even louder.

21
00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:25.392
"Whoa!" Bobby said.

22
00:01:25.393 --> 00:01:32.009
"It's pouring now," Jason said. "What a cool storm!"

23
00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:37.444
"Stop talking about the thunderstorm!" Izzie snapped.

24
00:01:37.445 --> 00:01:40.434
Her friends looked surprised.

25
00:01:40.435 --> 00:01:46.493
"I mean, er . . . we should be busy cooking!"

26
00:01:46.494 --> 00:01:54.501
Chef nodded. "Let's keep working. We have to brown the beef now."

27
00:01:54.502 --> 00:01:58.385
He used a spoon to break up the beef in the pot.

28
00:01:58.386 --> 00:02:02.834
While it cooked, Izzie opened the can of beans.

29
00:02:02.835 --> 00:02:07.003
Nina held a strainer, and Izzie poured the beans into it.

30
00:02:07.004 --> 00:02:10.675
"We drained the liquid," Izzie said.

31
00:02:10.676 --> 00:02:15.452
"Next we rinse the beans and add them to the pot."

32
00:02:15.453 --> 00:02:20.236
"I'll add the can of tomatoes," Bobby said.

33
00:02:20.237 --> 00:02:25.287
Izzie looked at Chef. "Can we mix all the spices now?"

34
00:02:25.288 --> 00:02:28.743
"Sure. You're working fast today, Izzie."

35
00:02:28.744 --> 00:02:32.318
Chef pointed to the spices on the counter.

36
00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:35.129
Izzie quickly measured the chili powder.

37
00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:38.542
She poured it into a small bowl.

38
00:02:38.543 --> 00:02:42.911
Nina and Jason added cumin and oregano.

39
00:02:42.912 --> 00:02:46.373
Bobby put in the paprika.

40
00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:50.955
"Now we add the salt and pepper," Izzie said.

41
00:02:50.956 --> 00:02:54.789
Nina mixed all the spices together.

42
00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.652
Then Chef added the mix to the chili and stirred.

43
00:02:58.653 --> 00:03:04.040
"The chili simmers on low heat for twenty minutes," Jason said.

44
00:03:04.041 --> 00:03:18.202
"Right," Chef said. "The spices will add flavor as it simmers."

45
00:03:18.203 --> 00:03:24.298
Bobby smiled. "Let's tell ghost stories while we wait!"

46
00:03:24.299 --> 00:03:30.308
"No!" Izzie said. "We have to clean up first."

47
00:03:30.309 --> 00:03:37.147
"Yep." Jason started washing dishes.

48
00:03:37.148 --> 00:03:41.245
"I'll help you, Jason," Izzie said.

49
00:03:41.246 --> 00:03:44.914
"We can all help with the chores," Chef said.

50
00:03:44.915 --> 00:03:47.702
He put on some music.

51
00:03:47.703 --> 00:03:52.050
Soon everyone was busy, cleaning up the kitchen.

52
00:03:52.051 --> 00:03:56.861
A few minutes later, a flash of lightning lit up the windows.

53
00:03:56.862 --> 00:04:00.431
A huge crack of thunder split the air.

54
00:04:00.432 --> 00:04:06.077
Jason jumped. "Yikes! That was loud!"

55
00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:10.638
"What?" Izzie looked up from the dish she was drying.

56
00:04:10.639 --> 00:04:14.210
"I didn't even hear it this time!"

57
00:04:14.211 --> 00:04:19.307
Chef grinned. "Sometimes it's good to stay busy."

58
00:04:19.308 --> 00:04:25.867
Izzie nodded. "Maybe I'll try it during the next thunderstorm," she thought.

59
00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:28.945
At last the timer went off.

60
00:04:28.946 --> 00:04:32.946
Chef filled five bowls with steaming chili.

61
00:04:32.947 --> 00:04:38.117
Nina looked out the window. "The storm is over!"

62
00:04:38.118 --> 00:04:41.054
Izzie sighed with relief.

63
00:04:41.055 --> 00:04:44.797
Then she blew on her chili to cool it off.

64
00:04:44.798 --> 00:04:49.265
"It's delicious!" she said, tasting it.

65
00:04:49.266 --> 00:04:52.883
A ray of sunshine shone through the window.

66
00:04:52.884 --> 00:05:00.932
"And look! There's a rainbow!" Izzie said.

